# Chrome extension: a content_security_policy that allows unsafe-eval or
# unsafe-inline defeats the purpose of the CSP and is disallowed in MV3.
# @see docs/rules-authoring.md
id: CHROME-SEC-005
ilities: [integrity]
maturity: 3
title: Chrome extension CSP allows unsafe-eval / unsafe-inline
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
action: block
confidence: 0.85
target:
  filenames: manifest.json
  content_contains: content_security_policy
patterns:
  - regex: unsafe-eval
    message: "CSP 'unsafe-eval' allows dynamic code execution — disallowed in MV3. Remove it."
  - regex: unsafe-inline
    message: "CSP 'unsafe-inline' allows inline scripts (XSS risk) — remove it; move scripts to files."
fix: "Remove unsafe-eval/unsafe-inline; use external script files and hashes/nonces if needed."
